#X msg 110 626 apin_mapping?;
#X text 245 626 query mapping between analog port number and digital
pin. Analog messages are numbered 0 to 15 \, which traditionally refer
to the Arduino pins labeled A0 \, A1 \, A2 \, etc. However \, these
pis are actually configured using "normal" pin numbers in the pin mode
message \, and when those pins are used for non-analog functions. The
analog mapping query provides the information about which pins (as
used with Firmata's pin mode message) correspond to the analog channels.
Return sequence of messages like: [apin_mapping A# PIN#( \, where #
is number.;
#X msg 110 787 capabilities?;
#X text 245 787 query pin capabilities. Return sequence of messages
like: [pin_info PIN# MODE RESOLUTION( \, where # is pin number.;
#X msg 110 827 firmware?;
#X text 245 827 query firmata protocol version. Returns message like:
[firmware ARDUINO_FIRMWARE_NAME.ino MAJOR MINOR(.;
#X msg 110 867 pin_mode;
#X text 245 867 sets pin mode. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 890 cnv 1 37 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 890 PIN#: pin number. Тип: int. Минимальное значение: 0\.;
#X obj 255 913 cnv 1 38 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 913 MODE: pin mode. Тип: symbol. Разрешённые значения:
INPUT \, OUTPUT \, ANALOG \, PWM \, SERVO \, SHIFT \, I2C \, ONEWIRE
\, STEPPER \, ENCODER \, SERIAL \, PULLUP.;
#X msg 110 968 pin_state?;
#X text 245 968 query pin state. The pin state is any data written
to the pin (it is important to note that pin state != pin value). For
output modes (digital output \, PWM \, and Servo) \, the state is any
value that has been previously written to the pin. For input modes
\, typically the state is zero. However \, for digital inputs \, the
state is the status of the pull-up resistor which is 1 if enabled \,
0 if disabled. Returns message like [pin_state PIN# MODE state( \,
where # is pin number. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 1127 cnv 1 37 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1127 PIN#: pin number. Тип: int.;
#X msg 110 1152 report_apin;
#X text 245 1152 turns on/off analog pin (A0-A6) value reporting. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 1175 cnv 1 83 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1175 ANALOG_PIN: analog pin number. Тип: int.;
#X obj 255 1198 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1198 VALUE: value. If 1 - activates analog reporting \,
messages like [apin PIN# value( are returned every sampling interval
(by default 19ms). Тип: int. Разрешённые значения: 0 \, 1\.;
#X msg 110 1253 report_dport;
#X text 245 1253 turns on/off digital port value reporting. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 1276 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1276 PORT#: digital port number. Port is a group of pins
\, port 0 refers pins 0-8\. Тип: int.;
#X obj 255 1314 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1314 VALUE: value. If 1 - activates digital port reporting
\, messages like [dport PORT# value( are returned only on pin value
change. Тип: int. Разрешённые значения: 0 \, 1\.;
#X msg 110 1369 samp_interval;
#X text 245 1369 sets sampling interval - how often analog data and
i2c data is reported to the client. The default for the arduino implementation
is 19ms. This means that every 19ms analog data will be reported and
any i2c devices with read continuous mode will be read. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 1468 cnv 1 38 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1468 TIME: time. Тип: int. Диапазон: 10…10000\. Единицы:
'ms'.;
